BCMS Starter Kit for ISO 22301
Free, editable templates for a business continuity management system (BCMS) under ISO 22301:2019, including Amendment 1:2024, from Brivellis.
Version 1.0 · October 2026 · 14 files · Free for use within one organisation
What's inside
#	File	Format
00	Read Me First	Document
00a	Responsible AI Use Guide	Document
01	BCMS Scope and Policy	Document
02	Business Impact Analysis Workbook	Workbook
03	Continuity Risk Assessment	Workbook
04	Strategy and Solutions Register	Workbook
05	Business Continuity Plan	Document
06	IT Disaster Recovery Runbook	Document
07	Exercise and Test Pack	Document
07	Exercise and Test Tracker	Workbook
08	Evidence Register and Management Review	Workbook
09	Crosswalk to ISO/IEC 27001:2022, ISO/IEC 20000-1:2018 and NIST SP 800-34 Rev. 1	Workbook
10	AI Tailoring Prompt Pack	Document
11	AI-Use Log	Workbook
The files work as one chain: business impact analysis → risk → strategies → plans → exercises → evaluation and review. Recovery targets (RTO and RPO) are set once, in the analysis; the strategy register checks every recovery option against them and flags any gap. Every file carries a worked example for a fictional company, Falcon Ridge IT Services, including one gap shown on purpose.
Download
Download the zip from the latest release. Kit page: https://brivellis.com/resources/bcms-starter-kit-iso-22301/
Before you use it
You need a licensed copy of ISO 22301:2019 including Amendment 1:2024. The kit refers to clause numbers with short descriptions in our own words; it does not reproduce the standard.
The crosswalk is a Brivellis mapping, not an official ISO or NIST mapping. NIST SP 800-34 Rev. 1 is cited by section title with attribution; NIST does not endorse this kit.
These are templates, not legal, certification or audit advice.
